    <title>Food Physics: Heat Transfer in Cooking</title>
    <content>
<![CDATA[
<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM 'http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd'>
<en-note>
<h2>Heat transfer</h2>
<p>Cooking relies on heat transfer. The three main modes are:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Conduction</b> (direct contact)</li>
  <li><b>Convection</b> (movement in fluids)</li>
  <li><b>Radiation</b> (electromagnetic waves)</li>
</ul>
<p>Reference: <a href="https://med.libretexts.org/Courses/Monterey_Peninsula_College/NUTF_10:_Food_Science/05:_Food_Preparation/5.01:_Food_Preparation/5.1.05:_Understanding_Heat">LibreTexts: Understanding Heat</a></p>
</en-note>
]]>
